namespace CarArchive.Core;
public static class IdentityFieldContract
{
    public const string Instructions="Generation is mandatory for an identified car: return the ordinal of its continuous base-series lineage (1st, 2nd, 3rd...), including 1st when only one generation exists; never omit it just because the name is unique, and never replace it with a chassis code or year. For derivatives count the underlying base series, not a restarted trim/body lineage. Audit how many distinct exterior facelifts the identified generation received, separating regional versions from successive revisions and using sources when search is enabled. Phase must identify the observed revision: Pre-Facelift before any facelift; Facelift only when that generation has exactly one facelift; otherwise 1st Facelift, 2nd Facelift, 3rd Facelift, etc. Never call every updated version Facelift when there are multiple revisions. Do not infer total facelift count from one photographed or archived example. If identity or revision is genuinely unresolved leave that field empty rather than inventing a fact.";
}
